# SocialLink API

Users can attach up to one link per platform to their ICPay profile.

Supported platforms: `github`, `linkedin`, `website`

Website domains allowed: `.com`, `.app`, `.ai`, `.shop`, `.net`, `.io`

---

## Design constraints

**No new storage module.** Social links are per-user metadata — they belong on
the `User` record. A separate map would duplicate a lookup that already exists.

**Field added to `User`**: `socialLinks: [SocialLink]` — a small array, one
entry per platform (max 3). Adding a field to a stable record needs a migration
(the upgrade-safety rule in the backend skill). Pattern is established in
`migrations/StampLedgerId.mo`.

**Candid forward-compatibility.** `UserPublic` is decoded by every client. The
new field must be `opt [SocialLink]` in the Candid interface so old frontends
decode it as `null` and new ones get the array. In Motoko: `?[SocialLink]`.

---

## Types (types.mo)

```motoko
public type SocialPlatform = { #github; #linkedin; #website };

public type SocialLink = {
  platform: SocialPlatform;
  url: Text;
};
```

`UserPublic` gets: `socialLinks: ?[SocialLink]`

---

## Validator (validators/SocialLinkValidator.mo)

Pure function returning `?Text` on failure — matches the validator convention.

```
validate(platform, url) -> ?Text
  must start with https://
  github   -> must contain github.com/
  linkedin -> must contain linkedin.com/in/
  website  -> TLD must be in: .com .app .ai .shop .net .io
              reject bare IPs and localhost
```

---

## Service (services/SocialLinkService.mo)

Takes `users: UserStorage.UserMap` only — no new storage.

```
setSocialLink(service, caller, platform, url) -> ApiResult<UserPublic>
  1. validate url
  2. getByPrincipal -> #err "User not found"
  3. upsert: replace entry for this platform, or append if absent
  4. return updated UserPublic

removeSocialLink(service, caller, platform) -> ApiResult<UserPublic>
  1. getByPrincipal
  2. filter out the entry for this platform
  3. return updated UserPublic
```

---

## API (api/v1/SocialLink.mo)

```motoko
setSocialLink(platform: SocialPlatform, url: Text) : async ApiResult<UserPublic>
removeSocialLink(platform: SocialPlatform)         : async ApiResult<UserPublic>
```

`getSocialLinks` is not needed — `getUser()` already returns `UserPublic` which
includes `socialLinks`.

---

## Migration

`User` gains `socialLinks: [SocialLink]`. The `with migration = ...` clause on
the `users` stable variable in `main.mo` rewrites every existing row, setting
`socialLinks = []`. Pattern: `migrations/StampLedgerId.mo`.

